Why `synapse_engine/logger.py` exists
--------------------------------------
Upstream `gllm/` does `from logger import logger` in ~22 files, expecting
a third-party PyPI package literally named `logger`. GreenBoost ships its
own stdlib-only shim of that name instead (see synapse_engine/logger.py)
so the vendored code needs zero source edits and pulls one fewer
dependency. `logger` is dropped from this package's own requirements for
that reason — see synapse_engine/pyproject.toml.
